@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `vn13-nouns`
IMPORT `vn13-fixtures`
IMPORT `vn13-art01-02-definitions`
IMPORT `vn13-art03-benefits`
IMPORT `vn13-art04-08-conditions`
IMPORT `vn13-art09-10-premiums`
IMPORT `vn13-art14-20-general`

-- Tests for the cover: Articles 1 to 8 and 14 to 20, and what a death claim pays.
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the text before the assertion was run; the
-- working is in the comment above each group. A failing assertion is a finding, never a
-- value to edit. Scenario figures (premiums, prices) are hypothetical; see vn13-fixtures.l4.

§ `Tests — cover`

§§ `Article 1 — eligibility and Age`

-- Age at the last birthday: born 20 June 1990, 35 on the eve of the 2026 birthday, 36 on it.
#ASSERT `the Age of a person born on` (YMD 1990 6 20) `on` (YMD 2026 6 19) EQUALS 35
#ASSERT `the Age of a person born on` (YMD 1990 6 20) `on` (YMD 2026 6 20) EQUALS 36
-- Born 29 February 2000: the birthday is taken as 28 February in a common year.
#ASSERT `the Age of a person born on` (YMD 2000 2 29) `on` (YMD 2026 2 27) EQUALS 25
#ASSERT `the Age of a person born on` (YMD 2000 2 29) `on` (YMD 2026 2 28) EQUALS 26

-- Issue ages 18 to 65, both ends in, on the issue date 15 January 2026.
#ASSERT `Article 1 — the Life Insured may be insured by a contract issued on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `, being` (`a resident Policyholder born on` (YMD 2008 1 15))
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 1 — the Life Insured may be insured by a contract issued on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `, being` (`a resident Policyholder born on` (YMD 2008 1 16)))
#ASSERT `Article 1 — the Life Insured may be insured by a contract issued on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `, being` (`a resident Policyholder born on` (YMD 1960 1 16))
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 1 — the Life Insured may be insured by a contract issued on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `, being` (`a resident Policyholder born on` (YMD 1960 1 15)))
-- Not resident in Vietnam at issue; not the Policyholder.
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 1 — the Life Insured may be insured by a contract issued on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `, being` (`The Life Insured` WITH `date of birth` IS YMD 1990 6 20, `resident in Vietnam on the issue date` IS FALSE, `the same person as the Policyholder` IS TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 1 — the Life Insured may be insured by a contract issued on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `, being` (`The Life Insured` WITH `date of birth` IS YMD 1990 6 20, `resident in Vietnam on the issue date` IS TRUE, `the same person as the Policyholder` IS FALSE))

§§ `Article 1 — values and dates`

GIVEN v IS A `A valuation of the account`
GIVETH A DATE
`the date of` v MEANS v's `valuation date`

GIVEN v IS A `A valuation of the account`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the account value in` v MEANS `the total account value of` (v's `holdings`)

-- Account value 10,000 x 15,000 + 5,000 x 10,000 = 200,000,000; with debt 2,000,000 on
-- 13 March: 10,000 x 16,000 + 5,000 x 10,200 = 211,000,000, surrender value 209,000,000.
#ASSERT `the account value in` (`a valuation on` (YMD 2030 3 6) `: Growth` 10_000 `at` 15_000 `, Balanced` 5_000 `at` 10_000 `, premium debt` 0) EQUALS 200_000_000
#ASSERT `the surrender value on` (`a valuation on` (YMD 2030 3 13) `: Growth` 10_000 `at` 16_000 `, Balanced` 5_000 `at` 10_200 `, premium debt` 2_000_000) EQUALS 209_000_000
-- A debt larger than the account: the definition gives a negative figure (it has no floor).
#ASSERT `the surrender value on` (`a valuation on` (YMD 2030 3 6) `: Growth` 0 `at` 15_000 `, Balanced` 0 `at` 10_000 `, premium debt` 1_000) EQUALS 0 MINUS 1_000
-- Premium debt: unpaid premiums 3,000,000 plus interest 150,000.
#ASSERT `the premium debt of` 3_000_000 `with interest of` 150_000 EQUALS 3_150_000

-- The next Valuation Date after a date is strictly after it: after Sunday 10 March 2030 it
-- is 13 March; after 13 March itself it is 20 March. Nothing after 20 March: a refusal.
#ASSERT `the date of` (`the valuation on the next Valuation Date after` (YMD 2030 3 10) `among` `the valuations of March 2030`) EQUALS YMD 2030 3 13
#ASSERT `the date of` (`the valuation on the next Valuation Date after` (YMD 2030 3 13) `among` `the valuations of March 2030`) EQUALS YMD 2030 3 20
#ASSERT REFUSED `the valuation on the next Valuation Date after` (YMD 2030 3 20) `among` `the valuations of March 2030` BECAUSE "no valuation on a Valuation Date after the date was supplied"
-- The list is out of order; the earliest later date is found all the same.
#ASSERT `the date of` (`the valuation on the next Valuation Date after` (YMD 2028 1 15) `among` `the valuations of 2027 and 2028`) EQUALS YMD 2028 1 19

-- Policy years from the Effective Date 10 January 2026.
#ASSERT `the policy year in which` (YMD 2026 1 10) `falls, for a contract effective on` (YMD 2026 1 10) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the policy year in which` (YMD 2027 1 9)  `falls, for a contract effective on` (YMD 2026 1 10) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the policy year in which` (YMD 2027 1 10) `falls, for a contract effective on` (YMD 2026 1 10) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the policy anniversary number` 15 `of a contract effective on` (YMD 2026 1 10) EQUALS YMD 2041 1 10
-- A monthly anniversary from 31 January falls on the last day of February.
#ASSERT `the monthly anniversary number` 1 `of a contract effective on` (YMD 2026 1 31) EQUALS YMD 2026 2 28

§§ `Article 1 — premiums and the loyalty bonus amount`

-- Total regular premium 20,000,000 + riders 1,000,000.
#ASSERT `the total regular premium in` `the schedule` EQUALS 21_000_000
-- Allocated premium: 20,000,000 less an initial charge of 18,000,000.
#ASSERT `the allocated premium, of a premium of` 20_000_000 `less an initial charge of` 18_000_000 EQUALS 2_000_000
-- Annualised: annual 20,000,000; monthly 2,000,000 x 12; quarterly 5,000,000 x 4;
-- half-yearly 10,000,000 x 2.
#ASSERT `the annualised regular basic premium at issue, in` `the schedule` EQUALS 20_000_000
#ASSERT `the annualised regular basic premium at issue, in` (`the schedule with a premium of` 2_000_000 `paid as` `monthly premiums`) EQUALS 24_000_000
#ASSERT `the annualised regular basic premium at issue, in` (`the schedule with a premium of` 5_000_000 `paid as` `quarterly premiums`) EQUALS 20_000_000
#ASSERT `the annualised regular basic premium at issue, in` (`the schedule with a premium of` 10_000_000 `paid as` `half-yearly premiums`) EQUALS 20_000_000
-- Loyalty bonus 360%: 20,000,000 x 3.6 = 72,000,000; monthly 24,000,000 x 3.6 = 86,400,000.
#ASSERT `the loyalty bonus for` `the schedule` EQUALS 72_000_000
#ASSERT `the loyalty bonus for` (`the schedule with a premium of` 2_000_000 `paid as` `monthly premiums`) EQUALS 86_400_000

§§ `Article 2 — changes`

#ASSERT `Article 2 — the change takes effect` (`A change to the contract` WITH `in writing` IS TRUE, `signed by the General Director or a Deputy General Director` IS TRUE, `with the Policyholder's consent` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 2 — the change takes effect` (`A change to the contract` WITH `in writing` IS TRUE, `signed by the General Director or a Deputy General Director` IS FALSE, `with the Policyholder's consent` IS TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 2 — the change takes effect` (`A change to the contract` WITH `in writing` IS TRUE, `signed by the General Director or a Deputy General Director` IS TRUE, `with the Policyholder's consent` IS FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 2 — the Company may be bound through a representative or third party` FALSE)

§§ `Article 3.1 — the death benefit`

-- The main claim: sum assured 500,000,000 + surrender value on 13 March 209,000,000
-- + risk and rider premiums after the death 300,000 + rider benefits 50,000,000
-- - premium debt 2,000,000 = 757,300,000. (The debt is in the surrender value already;
-- see NOTES.md findings.)
#ASSERT `Article 3.1 — the death benefit on` `the main claim` EQUALS 757_300_000
#ASSERT `what the Company pays on` `the main claim` EQUALS `the death benefit under Article 3.1` 757_300_000
-- In a grace period with 150,000 of risk premium and policy fee unpaid: 757,150,000.
#ASSERT `what the Company pays on` (`the main claim with history` `a clean history` `, first claimed` (YMD 2030 3 3) `, unpaid in grace` 150_000) EQUALS `the death benefit under Article 3.1` 757_150_000

§§ `Article 3.2 — exclusions`

-- (i) the Life Insured's own offence: the surrender value 209,000,000 less the debt
-- 2,000,000 = 207,000,000. Near miss: an offence by another person (a murder victim) is not
-- the exclusion on the reading taken, and the full benefit is paid.
#ASSERT `Article 3.2 — the death is excluded:` (`the main claim with own offence` TRUE `, other's offence` FALSE `, AIDS` FALSE)
#ASSERT `what the Company pays on` (`the main claim with own offence` TRUE `, other's offence` FALSE `, AIDS` FALSE) EQUALS `the surrender value under Article 3.2` 207_000_000
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 3.2 — the death is excluded:` (`the main claim with own offence` FALSE `, other's offence` TRUE `, AIDS` FALSE))
#ASSERT `what the Company pays on` (`the main claim with own offence` FALSE `, other's offence` TRUE `, AIDS` FALSE) EQUALS `the death benefit under Article 3.1` 757_300_000
-- (ii) AIDS, ARC or HIV: excluded, 207,000,000; near miss: not related, 757,300,000.
#ASSERT `what the Company pays on` (`the main claim with own offence` FALSE `, other's offence` FALSE `, AIDS` TRUE) EQUALS `the surrender value under Article 3.2` 207_000_000
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 3.2 — the death is excluded:` `the main claim`)

§§ `Article 3.3 — the loyalty bonus`

-- The 15th anniversary of 10 January 2026 is 10 January 2041.
#ASSERT `Article 3.3 — the 15th policy anniversary of a contract effective on` (YMD 2026 1 10) EQUALS YMD 2041 1 10

-- The fourth condition, tested at each withdrawal before the anniversary.
-- top-up 10,000,000 on 1 Jan 2030, withdrawal 10,000,000 on 1 Jan 2035: equal, so kept.
#ASSERT `Article 3.3 — the withdrawals never exceeded the top-ups, among` (LIST (`a top-up premium paid` (YMD 2030 1 1) 10_000_000), (`a withdrawal of account value` (YMD 2035 1 1) 10_000_000)) `, before` (YMD 2041 1 10)
-- one dong more: lost.
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 3.3 — the withdrawals never exceeded the top-ups, among` (LIST (`a top-up premium paid` (YMD 2030 1 1) 10_000_000), (`a withdrawal of account value` (YMD 2035 1 1) 10_000_001)) `, before` (YMD 2041 1 10))
-- a withdrawal the day before the top-up that covers it: lost ("at any time").
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 3.3 — the withdrawals never exceeded the top-ups, among` (LIST (`a top-up premium paid` (YMD 2030 1 1) 10_000_000), (`a withdrawal of account value` (YMD 2029 12 31) 5_000_000)) `, before` (YMD 2041 1 10))
-- top-up and withdrawal on the same day: the top-up counts ("up to the time of withdrawal").
#ASSERT `Article 3.3 — the withdrawals never exceeded the top-ups, among` (LIST (`a top-up premium paid` (YMD 2030 1 1) 10_000_000), (`a withdrawal of account value` (YMD 2030 1 1) 10_000_000)) `, before` (YMD 2041 1 10)
-- a withdrawal after the 15th anniversary does not count.
#ASSERT `Article 3.3 — the withdrawals never exceeded the top-ups, among` (LIST (`a withdrawal of account value` (YMD 2041 1 10) 50_000_000)) `, before` (YMD 2041 1 10)

-- All five conditions, and each one failing alone.
GIVEN `in force`       IS A BOOLEAN
      `paid in full`   IS A BOOLEAN
      `ever ended`     IS A BOOLEAN
      `ever on holiday` IS A BOOLEAN
      `withdrew`       IS A NUMBER
      `reduced`        IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The facts for the loyalty bonus`
`bonus facts: in force` `in force` `, paid in full` `paid in full` `, ever ended` `ever ended` `, holiday` `ever on holiday` `, withdrew` `withdrew` `, reduced` `reduced` MEANS
    `The facts for the loyalty bonus` WITH
        `the schedule at issue`                                    IS `the schedule`
        `in force at the 15th policy anniversary`                  IS `in force`
        `every regular basic premium paid in full over the years`  IS `paid in full`
        `ever ended as Article 20 describes`                       IS `ever ended`
        `ever on a premium holiday`                                IS `ever on holiday`
        `top-ups and withdrawals`                                  IS LIST (`a top-up premium paid` (YMD 2030 1 1) 10_000_000), (`a withdrawal of account value` (YMD 2035 1 1) `withdrew`)
        `sum assured ever reduced before the bonus`                IS `reduced`
        `valuations`                                               IS `the valuations of January 2041`

#ASSERT `Article 3.3 — the loyalty bonus is payable on` (`bonus facts: in force` TRUE `, paid in full` TRUE `, ever ended` FALSE `, holiday` FALSE `, withdrew` 10_000_000 `, reduced` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 3.3 — the loyalty bonus is payable on` (`bonus facts: in force` FALSE `, paid in full` TRUE `, ever ended` FALSE `, holiday` FALSE `, withdrew` 10_000_000 `, reduced` FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 3.3 — the loyalty bonus is payable on` (`bonus facts: in force` TRUE `, paid in full` FALSE `, ever ended` FALSE `, holiday` FALSE `, withdrew` 10_000_000 `, reduced` FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 3.3 — the loyalty bonus is payable on` (`bonus facts: in force` TRUE `, paid in full` TRUE `, ever ended` TRUE `, holiday` FALSE `, withdrew` 10_000_000 `, reduced` FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 3.3 — the loyalty bonus is payable on` (`bonus facts: in force` TRUE `, paid in full` TRUE `, ever ended` FALSE `, holiday` TRUE `, withdrew` 10_000_000 `, reduced` FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 3.3 — the loyalty bonus is payable on` (`bonus facts: in force` TRUE `, paid in full` TRUE `, ever ended` FALSE `, holiday` FALSE `, withdrew` 10_000_001 `, reduced` FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 3.3 — the loyalty bonus is payable on` (`bonus facts: in force` TRUE `, paid in full` TRUE `, ever ended` FALSE `, holiday` FALSE `, withdrew` 10_000_000 `, reduced` TRUE))

-- The units: bonus 72,000,000; on 11 January 2041 the Growth holding is 180,000,000 of
-- 240,000,000 (three quarters), so 54,000,000 at 18,000 = 3,000 units; the Balanced
-- holding 60,000,000 (a quarter), 18,000,000 at 12,000 = 1,500 units.
#ASSERT map (GIVEN c YIELD c's `units added`) (`Article 3.3 — the units of loyalty bonus on` (`bonus facts: in force` TRUE `, paid in full` TRUE `, ever ended` FALSE `, holiday` FALSE `, withdrew` 0 `, reduced` FALSE)) EQUALS LIST 3_000, 1_500

§§ `Article 4 — free look`

-- Documents received 20 January 2026: the last day is 10 February 2026.
#ASSERT `Article 4 — the last day of the free-look period, the documents being received on` (YMD 2026 1 20) EQUALS YMD 2026 2 10
#ASSERT `Article 4 — the Policyholder may refuse the contract by` (`a refusal given on` (YMD 2026 2 10) `, a benefit paid` FALSE `, documents returned` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 4 — the Policyholder may refuse the contract by` (`a refusal given on` (YMD 2026 2 11) `, a benefit paid` FALSE `, documents returned` TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 4 — the Policyholder may refuse the contract by` (`a refusal given on` (YMD 2026 2 1) `, a benefit paid` TRUE `, documents returned` TRUE))
-- Refund 21,000,000 less medical expenses 500,000; due only once the documents are back.
#ASSERT `Article 4 — the refund on` (`a refusal given on` (YMD 2026 2 1) `, a benefit paid` FALSE `, documents returned` TRUE) EQUALS 20_500_000
#ASSERT `Article 4 — the refund is due on` (`a refusal given on` (YMD 2026 2 1) `, a benefit paid` FALSE `, documents returned` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 4 — the refund is due on` (`a refusal given on` (YMD 2026 2 1) `, a benefit paid` FALSE `, documents returned` FALSE))
-- As a permission: refused on day 21, the Company's refund duty stands (no deadline);
-- refunded, all fulfilled; nothing done by day 22, the permission lapses harmlessly.
#TRACE `Article 4 — the free-look refusal and the refund` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Policyholder` DOES `refuse the contract by written notice` AT 21
#TRACE `Article 4 — the free-look refusal and the refund` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Policyholder` DOES `refuse the contract by written notice` AT 21
    PARTY `the Company` DOES `refund the premiums paid, less medical expenses` AT 90
#TRACE `Article 4 — the free-look refusal and the refund` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 22)

§§ `Article 5 — residence, travel, occupation`

#ASSERT NOT `Article 5 — residence, travel or occupation after issue restricts the cover`

§§ `Article 6 — age and sex`

-- Issued 15 January 2026. Truly born 1 January 1955: Age 71 at issue, outside 18 to 65.
-- Truly born 16 January 1960: 65, inside; born 15 January 1960: 66, outside.
#ASSERT `Article 6 —` (`a misstated birth date, truly` (YMD 1955 1 1) `, discovered` (YMD 2027 6 1)) `puts the true Age outside the insurable ages, the contract being issued on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 6 —` (`a misstated birth date, truly` (YMD 1960 1 16) `, discovered` (YMD 2027 6 1)) `puts the true Age outside the insurable ages, the contract being issued on` (YMD 2026 1 15))
#ASSERT `Article 6 —` (`a misstated birth date, truly` (YMD 1960 1 15) `, discovered` (YMD 2027 6 1)) `puts the true Age outside the insurable ages, the contract being issued on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
-- Truly born 16 January 2008: 17 at issue, outside; 15 January 2008: 18, inside.
#ASSERT `Article 6 —` (`a misstated birth date, truly` (YMD 2008 1 16) `, discovered` (YMD 2027 6 1)) `puts the true Age outside the insurable ages, the contract being issued on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 6 —` (`a misstated birth date, truly` (YMD 2008 1 15) `, discovered` (YMD 2027 6 1)) `puts the true Age outside the insurable ages, the contract being issued on` (YMD 2026 1 15))

-- Under two years from the Effective Date (10 January 2026 to 10 January 2028):
-- discovered 1 June 2027: 32,000,000 + 4,000,000 + 600,000 + surrender value on 4 June
-- 2027, 12,000,000, less medical 1,000,000 = 47,600,000.
#ASSERT `Article 6 — the payment for` (`a misstated birth date, truly` (YMD 1955 1 1) `, discovered` (YMD 2027 6 1)) `, effective from` (YMD 2026 1 10) `, having collected` `the charges collected` `, among` `the valuations of 2027 and 2028` EQUALS 47_600_000
-- Discovered 10 January 2028, the last day under two years: 36,600,000 + 13,000,000
-- (12 January 2028) - 1,000,000 = 48,600,000.
#ASSERT `Article 6 — the payment for` (`a misstated birth date, truly` (YMD 1955 1 1) `, discovered` (YMD 2028 1 10)) `, effective from` (YMD 2026 1 10) `, having collected` `the charges collected` `, among` `the valuations of 2027 and 2028` EQUALS 48_600_000
-- Discovered 11 January 2028: two years or more, the surrender value only, 13,000,000.
#ASSERT `Article 6 — the payment for` (`a misstated birth date, truly` (YMD 1955 1 1) `, discovered` (YMD 2028 1 11)) `, effective from` (YMD 2026 1 10) `, having collected` `the charges collected` `, among` `the valuations of 2027 and 2028` EQUALS 13_000_000
-- True age inside the ages: deductions of 4,000,000 recomputed at 3,500,000, so the
-- surrender value goes up by 500,000.
#ASSERT `Article 6 — the adjustment to the surrender value for` (`a misstated birth date, truly` (YMD 1960 1 16) `, discovered` (YMD 2027 6 1)) EQUALS 500_000
-- At a death: died 1 December 2027, discovered 6 December 2027, under two years:
-- 36,600,000 + 15,000,000 (8 December 2027) - 1,000,000 = 50,600,000.
#ASSERT `what the Company pays on` `a claim with a misstated age` EQUALS `the payment under Article 6` 50_600_000

§§ `Article 7 — incontestability`

-- Issued 15 January 2026: the two years run out on 15 January 2028.
#ASSERT `Article 7 — the day two years run out, for a contract issued on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `and last reinstated` NOTHING EQUALS YMD 2028 1 15
#ASSERT `Article 7 — the day two years run out, for a contract issued on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `and last reinstated` (JUST (YMD 2027 6 1)) EQUALS YMD 2029 6 1
-- A decision on 15 January 2028 is not yet barred; on 16 January it is (Life Insured alive).
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 7 — the Company may no longer contest` (`a non-disclosure, affecting underwriting` TRUE `, fraud` FALSE) `on` (YMD 2028 1 15) `, for a contract issued on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `, last reinstated` NOTHING `, the Life Insured dying` NOTHING)
#ASSERT `Article 7 — the Company may no longer contest` (`a non-disclosure, affecting underwriting` TRUE `, fraud` FALSE) `on` (YMD 2028 1 16) `, for a contract issued on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `, last reinstated` NOTHING `, the Life Insured dying` NOTHING
-- Fraud: never barred.
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 7 — the Company may no longer contest` (`a non-disclosure, affecting underwriting` TRUE `, fraud` TRUE) `on` (YMD 2035 1 1) `, for a contract issued on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `, last reinstated` NOTHING `, the Life Insured dying` NOTHING)
-- Death inside the two years: the two years never ran during the Life Insured's life.
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 7 — the Company may no longer contest` (`a non-disclosure, affecting underwriting` TRUE `, fraud` FALSE) `on` (YMD 2028 2 1) `, for a contract issued on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `, last reinstated` NOTHING `, the Life Insured dying` (JUST (YMD 2027 12 1)))
-- Reinstated 1 June 2027: the clock restarts, so a decision on 1 June 2028 is in time.
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 7 — the Company may no longer contest` (`a non-disclosure, affecting underwriting` TRUE `, fraud` FALSE) `on` (YMD 2028 6 1) `, for a contract issued on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `, last reinstated` (JUST (YMD 2027 6 1)) `, the Life Insured dying` NOTHING)
-- A misstatement of age or sex, or in a supplementary part: never barred.
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 7 — the Company may no longer contest` (`A non-disclosure or misstatement` WITH `could affect the underwriting decision` IS TRUE, `not itself disclosed by the Policyholder` IS TRUE, `about age or sex` IS TRUE, `in a supplementary part of the contract` IS FALSE, `insurance fraud` IS FALSE, `the Company's decision date` IS NOTHING) `on` (YMD 2035 1 1) `, for a contract issued on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `, last reinstated` NOTHING `, the Life Insured dying` NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 7 — the Company may no longer contest` (`A non-disclosure or misstatement` WITH `could affect the underwriting decision` IS TRUE, `not itself disclosed by the Policyholder` IS TRUE, `about age or sex` IS FALSE, `in a supplementary part of the contract` IS TRUE, `insurance fraud` IS FALSE, `the Company's decision date` IS NOTHING) `on` (YMD 2035 1 1) `, for a contract issued on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `, last reinstated` NOTHING `, the Life Insured dying` NOTHING)
-- The ground: affecting underwriting AND not itself disclosed.
#ASSERT `Article 7 — a ground to treat the contract as void is` (`a non-disclosure, affecting underwriting` TRUE `, fraud` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 7 — a ground to treat the contract as void is` (`a non-disclosure, affecting underwriting` FALSE `, fraud` FALSE))

-- At a death on 1 December 2027 (inside the two years), decided 1 February 2028: refund
-- 32,000,000 + 4,000,000 + 600,000 + the surrender value on 2 February 2028, 14,000,000
-- = 50,600,000.
#ASSERT `what the Company pays on` (`a claim for a death on` (YMD 2027 12 1) `, claimed on` (YMD 2027 12 5) `, with` (`a non-disclosure, affecting underwriting` TRUE `, fraud` FALSE)) EQUALS `the refund on avoidance under Article 7` 50_600_000
-- Near miss, no ground: the death benefit, 500,000,000 + 15,000,000 (8 December 2027).
#ASSERT `what the Company pays on` (`a claim for a death on` (YMD 2027 12 1) `, claimed on` (YMD 2027 12 5) `, with` (`a non-disclosure, affecting underwriting` FALSE `, fraud` FALSE)) EQUALS `the death benefit under Article 3.1` 515_000_000
-- Near miss, the Life Insured died on 20 January 2028, after the two years: barred, so the
-- death benefit, 500,000,000 + 16,000,000 (26 January 2028, after a claim on 22 January).
#ASSERT `what the Company pays on` (`a claim for a death on` (YMD 2028 1 20) `, claimed on` (YMD 2028 1 22) `, with` (`a non-disclosure, affecting underwriting` TRUE `, fraud` FALSE)) EQUALS `the death benefit under Article 3.1` 516_000_000

§§ `Article 8 — suicide`

-- Issued 15 January 2026: the two years end on 15 January 2028; with a reinstatement on
-- 1 June 2027, on 1 June 2029.
#ASSERT `Article 8 — the last day of the two years, for a contract issued on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `and last reinstated` NOTHING EQUALS YMD 2028 1 15
#ASSERT `Article 8 — the last day of the two years, for a contract issued on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `and last reinstated` (JUST (YMD 2027 6 1)) EQUALS YMD 2029 6 1
-- Suicide on 15 January 2028: within. Refund 36,600,000 + the surrender value on
-- 19 January 2028 (the next Valuation Date after the death), 15,000,000 = 51,600,000.
#ASSERT `what the Company pays on` (`an early death on` `a clean history` `, on` (YMD 2028 1 15) `, suicide` TRUE `, AIDS` FALSE) EQUALS `the refund under Article 8` 51_600_000
-- Suicide on 16 January 2028: outside. The death benefit: 500,000,000 + the surrender
-- value on 26 January 2028 (after the claim of 20 January), 16,000,000 = 516,000,000.
#ASSERT `what the Company pays on` (`an early death on` `a clean history` `, on` (YMD 2028 1 16) `, suicide` TRUE `, AIDS` FALSE) EQUALS `the death benefit under Article 3.1` 516_000_000
-- Lapsed 1 March 2027, reinstated 1 June 2027: suicide on 16 January 2028 is within.
#ASSERT `what the Company pays on` (`an early death on` (`a history with a lapse on` (YMD 2027 3 1) `and reinstatement` (JUST (YMD 2027 6 1))) `, on` (YMD 2028 1 16) `, suicide` TRUE `, AIDS` FALSE) EQUALS `the refund under Article 8` 51_600_000
-- Suicide within two years AND AIDS-related: Article 8 is applied first (fork register).
#ASSERT `what the Company pays on` (`an early death on` `a clean history` `, on` (YMD 2028 1 15) `, suicide` TRUE `, AIDS` TRUE) EQUALS `the refund under Article 8` 51_600_000
-- A death that is not a suicide, on 15 January 2028: the death benefit.
#ASSERT `what the Company pays on` (`an early death on` `a clean history` `, on` (YMD 2028 1 15) `, suicide` FALSE `, AIDS` FALSE) EQUALS `the death benefit under Article 3.1` 516_000_000

§§ `Articles 3 and 20 — in force at the death; Article 18 — time to claim`

